2026-05-25T02:13:08.716756Z  INFO ThreadId(10) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's what I found about the Phi-3.5-vision GGUF model for llama.cpp:\n\n## Current Status: Limited Support\n\n**The Phi-3.5-vision GGUF model exists but has compatibility issues with the main branch of llama.cpp.**\n\n### Available Model\nThere is a GGUF version available on Hugging Face:\n- **Repository**: `abetlen/Phi-3.5-vision-instruct-gguf`\n- **Model size**: 4B parameters\n- **Available quantizations**: Q8_0 (4.06 GB) and F16 (7.64 GB)\n- **Downloads**: ~1,300 per month\n\nHowever, the repository explicitly states: **\"work-in-progress does not currently work with main branch of llama.cpp\"**\n\n### Why the Compatibility Issue?\n\nAccording to discussions on the official Microsoft Phi-3.5-vision page, the model uses advanced techniques that aren't yet fully supported in llama.cpp:\n- **LongRoPE** (extended context handling)\n- **Flash Attention** \n- **CLIP ViT projector** (vision encoder architecture)\n\n### Current Workarounds\n\n1. **Use alternative runtimes**: Microsoft provides ONNX Runtime support for Phi-3.5 models, but this has its own limitations on certain platforms (like macOS x86).\n\n2. **Wait for llama.cpp updates**: The llama.cpp project is actively developing multimodal support. Recent additions include the `libmtmd` library and `llama-mtmd-cli` tool for vision models, but Phi-3.5-vision isn't yet in the list of officially supported models.\n\n3. **Try other Phi models**: Regular Phi-3.5-mini (text-only) works well with llama.cpp and is available in GGUF format from multiple sources like `lmstudio-community/Phi-3.5-mini-instruct-GGUF`.\n\n### How to Use When Supported\n\nOnce compatibility is achieved, you would use it like other multimodal models:\n\n```bash\n# With llama-server (when supported)\nllama-server -m phi-3.5-vision-instruct.gguf --mmproj mmproj-phi-3.5-vision.gguf\n\n# Or with the new mtmd system\nllama-mtmd-cli -hf abetlen/Phi-3.5-vision-instruct-gguf\n```\n\n### Recommendation\n\nFor now, if you need vision capabilities with llama.cpp, consider using officially supported models like:\n- LLaVA 1.5/1.6\n- Qwen2-VL / Qwen2.5-VL\n- Gemma 3\n- Moondream2\n- InternVL\n\nCheck the official llama.cpp multimodal documentation for the current list of supported vision models.\n\n**Sources**:\n- https://huggingface.co/abetlen/Phi-3.5-vision-instruct-gguf\n- https://huggingface.co/microsoft/Phi-3.5-vision-instruct/discussions/3\n- https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/docs/multimodal.md","type":"text"}],"id":"811caf05a2bc424095921f2c348231f3","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":31300,"input_tokens":20691,"output_tokens":669}}
