2026-05-25T02:14:06.137959Z  INFO ThreadId(10) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's a comprehensive overview of the current situation regarding DeepSeek-VL2, GGUF format, and llama.cpp multimodal support:\n\n## **DeepSeek-VL2 Overview**\nDeepSeek-VL2 is an advanced Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) Vision-Language Model series with three variants:\n- **DeepSeek-VL2-Tiny**: 1.0B activated parameters\n- **DeepSeek-VL2-Small**: 2.8B activated parameters  \n- **DeepSeek-VL2**: 4.5B activated parameters\n\nThe model excels at visual question answering, OCR, document/table/chart understanding, and visual grounding. It uses a dynamic tiling vision encoding strategy and DeepSeekMoE with Multi-head Latent Attention for efficient inference.\n\n## **Current GGUF/llama.cpp Status for DeepSeek-VL2**\n**Important limitation**: As of my current research, **DeepSeek-VL2 does NOT have official GGUF conversion or llama.cpp support**. The official DeepSeek-VL2 repository only provides PyTorch/HuggingFace implementations.\n\n## **llama.cpp Multimodal Support**\nllama.cpp **does support multimodal vision models** through its `libmtmd` system, but with limited model coverage:\n\n### **Currently Supported Vision Models in llama.cpp**:\n- **Gemma 3** (4B, 12B, 27B)\n- **SmolVLM** series\n- **Pixtral 12B**\n- **Qwen2-VL** and **Qwen2.5-VL** (2B, 7B, 32B, 72B)\n- **InternVL2.5** and **InternVL3**\n- **Llama 4 Scout**\n- **Moondream2**\n- **Mistral Small 3.1**\n\n### **How Multimodal Works in llama.cpp**:\n1. **Dual-file system**: Main text model (`.gguf`) + multimodal projector (`mmproj.gguf`)\n2. **Usage**: `llama-server -m model.gguf --mmproj mmproj.gguf`\n3. **CLI tool**: `llama-mtmd-cli` for command-line multimodal inference\n4. **API**: OpenAI-compatible `/chat/completions` endpoint with image support\n\n## **Alternative Approaches for DeepSeek-VL2**\n\n### **Option 1: Use Official PyTorch Implementation**\n```python\nfrom deepseek_vl2.models import DeepseekVLV2Processor, DeepseekVLV2ForCausalLM\nfrom deepseek_vl2.utils.io import load_pil_images\n\nmodel_path = \"deepseek-ai/deepseek-vl2-tiny\"\nvl_chat_processor = DeepseekVLV2Processor.from_pretrained(model_path)\nvl_gpt = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(model_path, trust_remote_code=True)\n```\n\n### **Option 2: Wait for Community Conversion**\nThe GGUF format is community-driven. You could:\n- Monitor the [llama.cpp repository](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) for DeepSeek-VL2 support\n- Check HuggingFace for community-converted GGUF versions\n- Contribute to adding support if you have the technical capability\n\n### **Option 3: Use Alternative Optimized Inference**\nThe official documentation recommends production deployment solutions:\n- **vLLM** - High-throughput serving\n- **SGLang** - Structured generation\n- **LMDeploy** - Efficient deployment\n\n## **Key Technical Challenges**\n1. **MoE Architecture**: DeepSeek-VL2 uses Mixture-of-Experts, which llama.cpp doesn't fully optimize for\n2. **Multi-head Latent Attention**: Special attention mechanism not yet supported in llama.cpp\n3. **Dynamic Tiling**: Complex vision encoding strategy requiring custom implementation\n\n## **Recommendation**\nFor now, use the official PyTorch implementation for DeepSeek-VL2. If you need GGUF/llama.cpp specifically, consider using one of the supported vision models like **Qwen2.5-VL** or **InternVL3**, which offer similar capabilities and are optimized for local inference.\n\n**Sources**:\n- [DeepSeek-VL2 Official Repository](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-VL2)\n- [llama.cpp Multimodal Documentation](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/docs/multimodal.md)\n- [DeepSeek-VL2 Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.10302)","type":"text"}],"id":"85db7d5dd5004135a3b6aed40ce9454c","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":115976,"input_tokens":16641,"output_tokens":996}}
