2026-05-25T02:14:37.799755Z  INFO ThreadId(13) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's comprehensive information about **Gemma 3 vision with GGUF and llama.cpp multimodal support**:\n\n## Overview\n\nGemma 3 is Google's latest multimodal model family that handles both text and image inputs while generating text outputs. The models come in 1B, 4B, 12B, and 27B parameter sizes, with the 1B variant **not supporting vision**. Gemma 3 features a 128K context window (32K for 1B), multilingual support for 140+ languages, and is optimized for local deployment.\n\n## llama.cpp Support Status\n\nGemma 3 vision support in llama.cpp is **experimental** and intended primarily for demonstration purposes. The implementation requires:\n\n- A text model GGUF file\n- A separate `mmproj.gguf` (multimodal projection) file\n- The `llama-mtmd-cli` or `llama-gemma3-cli` binary\n\n## Quick Start Guide\n\n### 1. Build llama.cpp\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp.git\ncd llama.cpp\ncmake -B build\ncmake --build build --target llama-mtmd-cli\n# Or install via brew on MacOS: brew install llama.cpp\n```\n\n### 2. Download Pre-quantized Models\n\nYou can use models directly from Hugging Face:\n\n```bash\n# Using the official ggml-org models\nllama-mtmd-cli -hf ggml-org/gemma-3-4b-it-GGUF\nllama-mtmd-cli -hf ggml-org/gemma-3-12b-it-GGUF\nllama-mtmd-cli -hf ggml-org/gemma-3-27b-it-GGUF\n```\n\nAlternatively, download from community sources like [Mungert's Gemma 3 GGUF collection](https://huggingface.co/Mungert/gemma-3-4b-it-GGUF).\n\n### 3. Running with Images\n\n```bash\n# Interactive chat mode\nllama-gemma3-cli -m gemma-3-4b-it-q4_k_l.gguf --mmproj gemma-3-4b-it-mmproj-bf16.gguf\n\n# Available commands:\n# /image <path>    load an image\n# /clear           clear chat history\n# /quit or /exit   exit program\n\n# Or direct image processing\n./build/bin/llama-mtmd-cli -m {text_model}.gguf --mmproj mmproj.gguf --image your_image.jpg\n```\n\n## Model Files Required\n\n- **Text model GGUF**: Choose from various quantizations (Q4_K, Q6_K, Q8, BF16, F16, etc.)\n- **mmproj file**: The multimodal projection file (e.g., `mmproj-bf16.gguf`)\n\nExample file naming from Mungert's collection:\n- `google_gemma-3-4b-it-q4_k_l.gguf` (text model)\n- `google_gemma-3-4b-it-mmproj-bf16.gguf` (vision projection)\n\n## Converting Your Own Models\n\nIf you want to convert from the original Hugging Face model:\n\n```bash\ncd gemma-3-4b-it\npython ../llama.cpp/convert_hf_to_gguf.py --outfile model.gguf --outtype f16 --mmproj .\n# This generates: model.gguf and mmproj-model.gguf\n```\n\n## Model Sizes and Quantization Options\n\nAvailable formats range from ultra-low-bit (IQ1_S at ~8GB for 27B) to full precision (BF16 at ~18GB). For CPU inference, Q4_K offers good balance between size and accuracy. The 4B model quantizations range from 1.86GB (IQ3_XS) to 7.77GB (BF16).\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **Experimental**: This is cutting-edge technology and may have stability issues\n- **1B model limitation**: The 1B variant does not support vision capabilities\n- **Image preprocessing**: Images are normalized to 896×896 resolution and encoded to 256 tokens each\n- **Performance**: Image encoding/decoding can be time-consuming (example showed 46s encoding, 19s decoding)\n\n## Sources\n\n- [llama.cpp Gemma 3 Documentation](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/docs/multimodal/gemma3.md)\n- [Mungert's Gemma 3 4B GGUF](https://huggingface.co/Mungert/gemma-3-4b-it-GGUF)\n- [Mungert's Gemma 3 27B GGUF](https://huggingface.co/Mungert/gemma-3-27b-it-GGUF)\n- [Google AI Gemma Documentation](https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/core)","type":"text"}],"id":"fd57a499a33f4128961524097d53a72b","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":22888,"input_tokens":5268,"output_tokens":1084}}
