2026-05-26T02:04:17.744432Z  INFO ThreadId(16) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide a comprehensive answer about FlashAttention-4's requirements for building with CUTLASS CuTe DSL support for SM_120a (Blackwell consumer GPUs) as of 2026.\n\n## FlashAttention-4 CUTLASS CuTe DSL Requirements for SM_120a Blackwell\n\n### Key Requirements\n\n**Hardware Target:**\n- SM_120a (consumer Blackwell: RTX 5090, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, DGX Spark GB10)\n- Compute capability 12.0 with \"a\" suffix for MMA instructions\n\n**Software Stack:**\n- **CUDA Toolkit**: 12.8 or newer (13.0+ recommended for `compute_120f` full feature set)\n- **PyTorch**: 2.10.0+ with CUDA support\n- **CUTLASS**: 4.4.1+ (with CuTe DSL support)\n- **nvidia-cutlass-dsl**: >= 4.4.1 (auto-installed by kernels library)\n- **Additional dependencies**: einops, apache-tvm-ffi\n\n### Critical Build Considerations\n\n**Architecture Flags:**\n- Use `compute_120a` for MMA instruction support (CUDA 12.8+)\n- Use `compute_120f` for full feature set including TMA grouped GEMM (CUDA 13.0+ only)\n- Note: `sm_120` (without suffix) does NOT enable MMA instructions and will fail\n\n**CuTe DSL Architecture Support:**\nThe CuTe DSL must include `sm_120a` in admissible architectures across multiple files:\n- `cutlass/cute/nvgpu/cpasync/copy.py`\n- `cutlass/cute/nvgpu/tcgen05/mma.py`\n- `cutlass/cute/nvgpu/tcgen05/copy.py`\n- `cutlass/cute/arch/mbar.py`\n- `cutlass/cute/arch/elect.py`\n\n**Device Mapping:**\nAdd to `cuda.py`:\n```python\n(12, 0): (\"Blackwell\", \"sm_120a\", [\"sm_120a\"])\n```\n\n### Known Issues and Workarounds\n\n**CUTLASS Grouped GEMM Problems:**\nNative CUTLASS grouped block-scaled FP4 GEMM kernels produce garbage output on SM_120 due to broken templates. This affects MoE expert computations specifically.\n\n**FlashInfer CUTLASS Backend (Working Solution):**\nRequires patching 10+ files to enable SM_120 support:\n- Update capability checks to include family 120\n- Add `sm_120a` to CuTe DSL admissible archs\n- Modify JIT architecture filters to include major version 12\n- Patch TRT-LLM C++ launcher to use `>=` instead of `==` for major version checks\n\n**Performance:**\n- With `compute_120a` (CUDA 12.8): ~14.6 tok/s (slow due to TMA WS fallback)\n- With `compute_120f` (CUDA 13.0): ~39.0 tok/s (enables fast TMA tactics)\n- Marlin W4A16 workaround: ~46-49 tok/s (current production recommendation)\n\n### Installation Methods\n\n**Recommended (via kernels library):**\n```bash\npip install -U kernels\nfrom kernels import get_kernel\nflash_attn_4 = get_kernel(\"SecondNatureComputing/flash-attn-4-sm120\")\n```\n\n**Direct use:**\n```bash\ngit clone https://huggingface.co/SecondNatureComputing/flash-attn-4-sm120\n# Add to Python path and import\n```\n\n### Production Recommendation\n\nUntil `compute_120f` with CUDA 13.0 is fully validated, use Marlin backend for NVFP4 MoE models:\n```bash\npython -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \\\n  --model nvidia/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-NVFP4 \\\n  --moe-backend marlin \\\n  --tensor-parallel-size 2 \\\n  --pipeline-parallel-size 2\n```\n\n### Sources\n- [CUTLASS Issue #3096 - SM120 NVFP4 MoE Debug Report](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3096)\n- [FlashAttention-4 SM120 Bundle](https://huggingface.co/SecondNatureComputing/flash-attn-4-sm120)\n- [FlashAttention-4 Paper (arXiv:2603.05451)](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.05451v1)\n- [DeepWiki - FlashAttention Blackwell Architecture](https://deepwiki.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/4-blackwell-(sm100sm120)-architecture)","type":"text"}],"id":"9f10af3682b54bb9aed8a6c14535c772","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":62072,"input_tokens":6918,"output_tokens":1123}}
