2026-05-26T02:06:31.746804Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide comprehensive information about building xformers for Blackwell architecture (sm_120a) with CUDA 13.2 and FlashAttention support in 2026.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Current State (2026)\n\n**CUDA 13.2** is the current stable release as of May 2026, released on March 9, 2026. It supports Blackwell architecture including sm_120 (RTX 50 series) and sm_100 (datacenter Blackwell).\n\n### xformers Blackwell Support\n\nA community project has achieved the **first successful xformers compilation for RTX 5090 D (Blackwell sm_120)** using:\n- **CUDA 12.8** (not 13.2 yet)\n- **PyTorch 2.9.0** nightly with CUDA 12.8\n- **xformers 0.0.32** with custom patches\n\nKey technical achievements include:\n- CUTLASS 4.0 integration with Blackwell support\n- Sparse24 compatibility fixes\n- memory_efficient_attention fully functional\n- Performance up to 61.1M tokens/sec on XL scale\n\n### FlashAttention Status\n\nFlashAttention support for Blackwell is still in development. The main FlashAttention repository (Dao-AILab/flash-attention) has an open issue (#1987) requesting Blackwell (sm_120) support, with users reporting errors when trying to use FlashAttention forward/backward kernels on Blackwell GPUs.\n\n## Building xformers with CUDA 13.2 for sm_120a\n\nBased on the available information, here's what you need to know:\n\n### Prerequisites\n- **GPU**: NVIDIA RTX 5090/5080/5070 (Blackwell, sm_120a)\n- **CUDA**: 13.2 (or 12.8 for proven compatibility)\n- **PyTorch**: 2.9.0+ with CUDA 13.2 support\n- **Python**: 3.12+\n- **OS**: Ubuntu 24.04+ or WSL2\n\n### Compilation Steps\n\n1. **Set environment variables**:\n```bash\nexport TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=\"12.0\"  # For sm_120\nexport FORCE_CUDA=1\nexport CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.2\n```\n\n2. **Install PyTorch with CUDA 13.2**:\n```bash\npip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/nightly/cu132\n```\n\n3. **Clone and patch xformers**:\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/facebookresearch/xformers.git\ncd xformers\n# Apply Blackwell patches (similar to those in the community project)\n```\n\n4. **Build from source**:\n```bash\npip install -v -e .\n```\n\n### Important Notes\n\n- **sm_120a vs sm_120**: The \"a\" suffix indicates architecture-specific features that are not forward or backward compatible. Use `sm_120` for general compatibility, `sm_120a` only if you need the specialized Blackwell features.\n- **CUDA 13.2 vs 12.8**: While CUDA 13.2 is available, most proven Blackwell builds currently use CUDA 12.8. CUDA 13.2 support is newer and may require additional patches.\n- **FlashAttention**: Full FlashAttention support for Blackwell is still in beta/development. You may need to use fallback kernels or wait for official support.\n\n### Performance Expectations\n\nBased on the community project's benchmarks on RTX 5090 D:\n- Small scale (2×1024×64): ~19.9M tokens/sec\n- Medium scale (2×2048×64): ~46.4M tokens/sec  \n- Large scale (1×4096×64): ~60.4M tokens/sec\n- XL scale (1×8192×64): ~61.1M tokens/sec\n- XXL scale (1×16384×64): ~42.0M tokens/sec\n\n### Resources\n\n- Community xformers Blackwell project: https://github.com/xiangxin2025cn/xformer-update-maxwell\n- FlashAttention Blackwell issue: https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/issues/1987\n- CUDA 13.2 Release Notes: https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/13.2.0/cuda-toolkit-release-notes/index.html\n- Blackwell Compatibility Guide: https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/blackwell-compatibility-guide/index.html\n\nThe field is rapidly evolving, so check for updates to both xformers and FlashAttention for official Blackwell support.","type":"text"}],"id":"84fe6a1bb39b416e897a45b34f76d08e","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{