2026-05-26T02:07:52.402313Z  INFO ThreadId(12) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide a comprehensive answer about building FlashAttention-4 for SM120 (consumer Blackwell) without CUTLASS.CuTe fallback mode.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**FlashAttention-4 cannot run natively on SM120 (RTX 5090/5070 Ti) without falling back to CUTLASS.CuTe or other workarounds.** This is due to a fundamental architectural difference between datacenter Blackwell (SM100) and consumer Blackwell (SM120):\n\n### Hardware Architecture Difference\n\n| Feature | SM100 (B200/B300) | SM120 (RTX 5090) |\n|---------|-----------------|-----------------|\n| Tensor Memory (TMEM) | ✅ Full `UTMA*`/`UTC*` ISA | ❌ Not present |\n| MMA Instruction | `UTCHMMA.2CTA` (TMEM-backed) | `HMMA.16816` (register-backed) |\n| 2CTA Clusters | ✅ | ❌ |\n| Warp-Specialized Kernels | ✅ (FA4 design target) | ❌ Cannot express |\n| FlashAttention-4 | ✅ | ❌ |\n\n### Technical Evidence\n\nFrom the investigation (March 2026):\n\n1. **Python gatekeepers** in `flash-attention` and `cutlass-dsl` explicitly block SM120 from reaching FA4's compilation path\n2. **NVVM MLIR compiler** rejects SM120 for `tcgen05` instructions (the TMEM-backed MMA family FA4 requires)\n3. **PTX assembler** (`ptxas`) explicitly rejects `tcgen05` instructions for SM120 target\n4. **SASS disassembly** confirms SM120 lacks the entire `UTMA*`/`UTC*` instruction family - the tensor memory hardware is physically absent\n\n### What Works on SM120\n\nFor consumer Blackwell GPUs, the following options are available:\n\n1. **FlashAttention-2** via Triton (default `flex_attention` backend) - still fast on 5090\n2. **Custom FP4 kernels** using inline PTX with `mma.sync` instructions (as demonstrated in the detailed kernel implementation article)\n3. **Marlin** backend for W4A16 quantization (46-49 tok/s in MoE workloads)\n4. **FlashInfer CUTLASS** with `compute_120f` (CUDA 13.0) - achieves 39 tok/s but requires extensive patching\n\n### Conclusion\n\n**There is no way to build FlashAttention-4 for SM120 without falling back to CUTLASS.CuTe or alternative implementations.** The \"Blackwell\" branding shared between RTX 5090 and B200/B300 obscures what are functionally different GPU architectures for compute workloads. SM120's tensor cores are powerful but architecturally closer to Hopper than to datacenter Blackwell.\n\nFor RTX 5090 users, FlashAttention-2 via Triton remains the best available attention kernel, though it will not benefit from FA4's tensor-memory-based optimizations.\n\nSources:\n- [FlashAttention-4 Cannot Run on RTX 5090 (SM120) — A Deep Investigation](https://gist.github.com/solatticus/aab6ec3a0436748b021cbbdd12e8c739)\n- [Building an FP4 Fused Attention Kernel on Consumer Blackwell (SM120)](https://florianmattana.com/posts/fp4-fused-attention-kernel-sm120/)\n- [FlashAttention-4: Algorithm and Kernel Pipelining Co-Design for Asymmetric Hardware Scaling](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.05451v1)\n- [CUTLASS Issue #3096 - SM120 (Bug) (With Fix) (RTX Blackwell) NVFP4 MoE](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3096)\n- [Flash Attention 4 (CuTe DSL) for SM120 / SM121 consumer Blackwell GPUs](https://huggingface.co/SecondNatureComputing/flash-attn-4-sm120)","type":"text"}],"id":"6bf44c4544a847f3bcacf7d857b758ea","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":57996,"input_tokens":55745,"output_tokens":967}}
