2026-05-26T13:23:33.022754Z  INFO ThreadId(17) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's the current status of Flash Attention support for RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (sm_120a) in 2026:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Official FlashAttention-4 Status\n**RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell does NOT support the full FlashAttention-4 kernel** due to fundamental hardware limitations. The GPU uses SM120 architecture (compute capability 12.0), which lacks the critical features that FA-4 requires:\n\n- **No TMEM** (Tensor Memory) - dedicated tensor memory subsystem\n- **No tcgen05** - new tensor instructions\n- **No WGMMA** (warp-group matrix multiply)\n- Limited to 99KB shared memory (vs 163KB on SM80)\n- Uses SM80-era `mma.sync` instructions instead\n\nThese hardware differences mean the RTX PRO 6000 falls back to FlashAttention-2 or older attention kernels, similar to how Ampere GPUs behave.\n\n### Community Solutions\nHowever, there are **workarounds available**:\n\n1. **SecondNatureComputing's flash-attn-4-sm120 bundle** - A downstream distribution that adapts FA4 kernels to SM120 constraints by bundling six upstream PRs:\n   - Supports paged KV cache, split-KV, block-sparse attention, dropout\n   - Performance is within 4-10% of FA2 on realistic sequence lengths\n   - Requires CUDA 12.8+ and specific dependencies\n\n2. **Autonomous optimization research** - Projects like `fa4-sm120-research` are actively tuning SM120 kernels, achieving up to 275 TFLOPS (92% utilization) with custom configurations.\n\n### Practical Implications for 2026\n\n- **vLLM/SGLang**: Official support for SM120 is maturing but may require building from source with proper CUDA arch flags (`TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=\"12.0 12.1\"`)\n- **Performance**: Expect similar attention performance to high-end Ampere/Ada GPUs, not the 1.5-2x gains seen on datacenter Blackwell (B200/SM100)\n- **Memory**: The 96GB VRAM is still valuable for large models, but attention kernel efficiency is limited\n\n### Recommendations\n\nIf you need cutting-edge attention performance, datacenter Blackwell (B200/B300) or Hopper (H100) GPUs are required. For workstation deployments where VRAM capacity matters more than peak attention throughput, the RTX PRO 6000 remains viable with the community FA4 adaptations.\n\n**Sources:**\n- https://www.hardware-corner.net/rtx-pro-6000-blackwell-flashattention-4/\n- https://huggingface.co/SecondNatureComputing/flash-attn-4-sm120\n- https://github.com/qu0b/fa4-sm120-research\n- https://discuss.vllm.ai/t/support-for-rtx-6000-blackwell-96gb-card/1707","type":"text"}],"id":"4bd75d68a46f4b8a89e94464493a06e4","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":47464,"input_tokens":1363,"output_tokens":685}}
